---
import LegalPageLayout from "../layouts/LegalPageLayout.astro";

const sectionClass = "grid gap-5 border-t border-white/35 py-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 lg:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]";
const copyClass = "max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-white/72 sm:text-base sm:leading-8";
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title="Service Terms | Monarchic"
  description="Terms for Monarchic accounts, hosted MCP routes, usage metering, billing, customer content, and service access."
  path="/terms"
  eyebrow="Legal / Service boundary"
  heading="Service Terms"
  introduction="These terms govern access to the Monarchic web app, hosted MCP routes, agent runs, and related paid or preview services."
  effectiveDate="July 21, 2026"
  documentId="service-terms"
  contactId="terms-contact"
>
  <a slot="toc" href="#agreement" class="hover:text-cyan-200">01 / Agreement</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#accounts" class="hover:text-cyan-200">02 / Accounts</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#usage" class="hover:text-cyan-200">03 / Usage</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#acceptable-use" class="hover:text-cyan-200">04 / Acceptable use</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#content" class="hover:text-cyan-200">05 / Content</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#billing" class="hover:text-cyan-200">06 / Billing</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#availability" class="hover:text-cyan-200">07 / Availability</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#risk" class="hover:text-cyan-200">08 / Risk</a>

  <section id="agreement" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">01</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Agreement and scope</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>By creating an account, using a hosted route, or buying a plan, you agree to these terms. If you use Monarchic for an organization, you confirm that you can bind that organization.</p>
        <p>An order form, checkout statement, or signed agreement may add product, support, security, pricing, or service terms. If it conflicts with this page, the signed or checkout-specific term controls for that order.</p>
        <p>You must be at least 18 years old. The service is built for professional and business use.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">02</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Accounts and access</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>Provide accurate account information and keep login credentials and API keys secure. You are responsible for activity under your account and for promptly revoking credentials that may be exposed.</p>
        <p>Access is tenant-scoped and may depend on plan, entitlement, role, route availability, and safety controls. Do not share access outside the organization or scope authorized by your plan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="usage" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">03</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Services and usage metering</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>Monarchic provides hosted MCP routes, agent execution, account controls, evidence artifacts, and related interfaces as described in current product documentation.</p>
        <p>Usage may be measured by operation class, runtime, external-provider work, storage, or another unit shown in the catalog or order. Credits are service units, have no cash value, and expire or reset as stated by the applicable plan. Metadata calls may be rated differently from infrastructure-backed work.</p>
        <p>Preview and coming-soon products are not available for checkout. Product labels and route status control over general marketing copy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">04</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Acceptable use</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>Use Monarchic only on systems, repositories, accounts, browsers, terminals, and data you are authorized to access. Follow applicable law and obtain required consent.</p>
        <p>Do not use the service to distribute malware, steal credentials, evade access controls, bypass CAPTCHAs, conduct unrestricted scraping, interfere with a service, harm a person, violate intellectual-property or privacy rights, or create an unreasonable security or infrastructure load.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for reviewing agent actions and setting appropriate scopes, approvals, rate limits, and human checks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="content" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">05</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Customer content and output</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>You keep ownership of content you submit. You grant Monarchic the limited rights needed to process, transmit, store, secure, and return that content while providing and supporting the service.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for having the rights to submit content and for deciding whether output is fit for use. Agent and model output can be incomplete, incorrect, or similar to output produced for someone else. Review it before deployment, publication, or any consequential decision.</p>
        <p>Monarchic retains its software, documentation, interfaces, product names, and other service materials. Feedback may be used without restriction or payment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="billing" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">06</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Billing</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>Prices, included usage, cadence, overage status, and taxes are shown at checkout or in an order. Stripe processes payment methods. Unless an order says otherwise, subscriptions renew for the selected cadence until canceled.</p>
        <p>You authorize charges shown at checkout and any enabled usage charges described by the plan. Failed or overdue payment may pause access. Fees are non-refundable except where the order or law requires otherwise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="availability" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">07</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Availability, suspension, and changes</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>We may change, limit, or discontinue a preview, route, model, integration, or feature. Published service-level commitments apply only when an order expressly includes them.</p>
        <p>We may suspend or terminate access for security risk, unlawful use, material breach, overdue payment, or harm to Monarchic, providers, or other users. You may stop using the service and cancel through the available account or billing controls.</p>
        <p>We may update these terms. Material changes will be posted here and, when appropriate, communicated through the account or email.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="risk" class={sectionClass}>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-cyan-200">08</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Warranty and liability boundary</h2>
      <div class={copyClass}>
        <p>Except for commitments in an applicable signed order, the service is provided as available and without warranties of uninterrupted operation, error-free output, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement, to the extent the law permits.</p>
        <p>To the extent the law permits, Monarchic is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data, goodwill, or business interruption. Monarchic's aggregate liability for the service will not exceed the amount you paid for that service during the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim.</p>
        <p>Some jurisdictions do not allow every exclusion or limit. In those places, the limits apply only as far as the law allows. These terms do not limit liability that cannot legally be limited.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div slot="contact">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-cyan-200">Questions about these terms</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Get the boundary clear before you run.</h2>
  </div>
  <div slot="contact" class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a href="mailto:support@monarchic.io?subject=Service%20terms" class="border-2 border-cyan-300 bg-cyan-300/10 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase text-cyan-100 transition hover:bg-cyan-300/20 hover:text-white">Contact support</a>
    <a href="/privacy" class="border-2 border-black px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase hover:bg-black hover:text-white">Read privacy</a>
  </div>
</LegalPageLayout>
